<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<div xmlns:ead="https://archivists.org/ns/ead/v4" xmlns:eac="http://archivists.org/ns/eac/v2" xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3c.org/1999/xlink" type="elementDocumentation" xml:id="elem-subject">
    <head>
        <gi>subject</gi>
    </head>
    <div type="fullName">
        <p>Subject</p>
    </div>
    <div type="summary">
        <p>An element for encoding controlled topics represented in the materials being described.</p>
    </div>
    <div type="mayContain">
        <p>
            <list type="gloss">
                <label>date or dateRange or dateSet</label>
                <item>0..1</item>
                <label>descriptiveNote</label>
                <item>0..1</item>
                <label>placeName</label>
                <item>0..n</item>
                <label>term</label>
                <item>1..n</item>
            </list>
        </p>
    </div>
    <div type="mayOccurWithin">
        <p>subjectHeadings</p>
    </div>
    <div type="attributes">
        <p>
            <list type="gloss">
                <label>audience</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>conventionDeclarationReference</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>id</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>languageOfElement</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>localType</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>localTypeDeclarationReference</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>maintenanceEventReference</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>scriptOfElement</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>sourceReference</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>target</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>valueURI</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>vocabularySource</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
                <label>vocabularySourceURI</label>
                <item>Optional</item>
            </list>
        </p>
    </div>
    <div type="description">
        <p>A <gi>subject</gi> element is a wrapper element used to encode an index term, using the required child element <gi>term</gi>. Terms are used to identify the topics and themes represented in the described materials. Such terms often provide useful access points to the materials, especially for corporate, government, or institutional records and may be drawn from controlled vocabularies or may be natural language terms.</p>
        <p>
            <gi>subject</gi> must include at least one <gi>term</gi> element. <gi>term</gi> can be repeated within <gi>subject</gi> to include translations of the same term. Use the <att>languageOfElement</att> attribute to identify the language used in each <gi>term</gi>.</p>
        <p>Associated date(s) (<gi>date</gi>, <gi>dateRange</gi>, or <gi>dateSet</gi>) and place(s) (<gi>placeName</gi>) may be included to further constrain the term's meaning. A <gi>descriptiveNote</gi> may be included if a fuller textual explanation is needed.</p>
        <p>A list of <gi>subject</gi> terms may also be used with reference pointers (<att>id</att> and <att>target</att>) to enhance navigation of and access to the materials being described.</p>
        <p>The order of child elements of <gi>subject</gi> is:
                  <list type="simple">
                <item>
                    <gi>term</gi>
                </item>
                <item>One of <gi>date</gi>, <gi>dateRange</gi>, or <gi>dateSet</gi>
                </item>
                <item>
                    <gi>placeName</gi>
                </item>
                <item>
                    <gi>descriptiveNote</gi>
                </item>
            </list>
        </p>
    </div>
    <div type="availability">
        <p>Optional, repeatable</p>
    </div>
    <div type="examples">
    </div>
</div>
